CALL newPutForth(288, 1, 'Cancel culture is real, it\'s organized, and it\'s doing serious damage. People lose their jobs, their platforms, their reputations — not because they did anything wrong, but because a mob decided they were ideologically impure. That\'s not accountability. That\'s intimidation.');
CALL newPutForth(289, 1, 'When professors self-censor because they\'re afraid of a student Twitter mob, science stops working. Academic freedom isn\'t a courtesy — it\'s the operating system for the kind of open inquiry that produces actual knowledge. Cancel culture is malware for that system.');
CALL newPutForth(291, 1, 'Your political opinions shouldn\'t cost you your livelihood. The moment we accept that employers should fire people for their private political beliefs, we\'ve handed a totalitarian lever to whichever political faction controls HR right now. That should scare both sides.');
CALL newPutForth(297, 1, 'Cancel culture isn\'t spontaneous — it\'s organized. It\'s a coordinated effort to enforce conformity with progressive norms by making deviation economically and socially costly. The goal isn\'t accountability. The goal is silence.');
CALL newPutForth(541, 1, 'There is no excuse to ban books. Not racism, not sexism, not offense, not discomfort. You don\'t fix a bad idea by hiding it — you fix it by exposing it and arguing against it. Libraries exist to preserve all of it, including the embarrassing parts.');
CALL newPutForth(595, 1, 'Speech doesn\'t pull a trigger. It doesn\'t punch a face. When we start criminalizing words, we hand whoever defines \'harmful speech\' a weapon against everyone else. The cure for bad speech is more speech, not silence.');
CALL newPutForth(596, 1, 'The right to free speech is absolute — or it isn\'t a right. The moment government or corporations decide which speech is \'acceptable,\' you don\'t have free speech anymore. You have permitted speech. That\'s a completely different thing.');
CALL newPutForth(599, 1, 'If liberal ideas were winning on the merits, they wouldn\'t need to deplatform their opponents. The entire cancel culture infrastructure exists because these ideas can\'t survive open debate. That\'s the tell.');
CALL newPutForth(600, 1, 'The Left cheered when conservatives got deplatformed, banned, and silenced. Now they\'re shocked — shocked — that people don\'t trust them as neutral arbiters of speech. You can\'t run a censorship machine for a decade and then claim to stand for free expression.');
CALL newPutForth(1431, 1, 'Comedy works by crossing lines. That\'s the art form. \'Only punch up, never down\' is a rule invented by people who wanted to protect themselves from jokes they didn\'t like, not by people who understand how humor actually works.');
CALL newPutForth(1562, 1, 'Woke ideology is turning every institution it touches into a political re-education exercise. Schools, corporations, the military, professional sports — all of it marinated in identity politics that nobody voted for. It has to stop.');
CALL newPutForth(1580, 1, 'The jokes that killed at family dinners five years ago are now career-ending confessions. That\'s not progress. That\'s a cultural panopticon where everybody self-monitors for thoughtcrime. It\'s not a kinder world — it\'s a more fearful one.');
CALL newPutForth(1582, 1, 'Mel Gibson, J.K. Rowling, Louis C.K., Dr. Seuss — at some point you have to ask what we\'re doing when we declare that people we once celebrated are now \'problematic.\' We\'re not getting better art or a better society. We\'re just burning things.');




